@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Phone pairing — a phone joins over Wi-Fi and gets its token
autonumber "<b>0"

actor User as user
participant "Console\nDevices tab (127.0.0.1:8000)" as devtab
participant "Ingest app\n(https://<laptop LAN IP>:8001)" as ingest
participant "PairingRequests\n(in memory, 5 min TTL)" as pairing
participant "TokenStore\n(devices.json, hashed, TTL 30 days)" as tokens
participant "Phone page\n(browser on the phone)" as phone

== Reach the laptop ==
user -> devtab : open Devices
devtab --> user : QR code + URL of the phone listener\n(the LAN or hotspot address, self-signed certificate)
user -> phone : scan the QR, accept the certificate
phone -> ingest : GET /
ingest -> pairing : seen(phone address)
ingest --> phone : phone page
devtab -> pairing : last_visit()
devtab --> user : step 2 of 4: "a phone opened the page"

== Ask to pair ==
phone -> ingest : POST /pair {device, label}
ingest -> pairing : open(device, label, address)
pairing --> ingest : PairRequest{id, 4-digit code, pending}
ingest --> phone : {request_id, code, status: pending}
phone --> user : shows the code
loop every second until decided
  phone -> ingest : GET /pair/{request_id}
  ingest -> pairing : collect(request_id)
  ingest --> phone : {status: pending}
end

== Approve on the laptop ==
devtab --> user : pending request: device, label, address, **code**
user -> devtab : the code matches → Approve\n(or Deny)
devtab -> pairing : approve(request_id)
pairing -> tokens : create(device)
tokens --> pairing : "bsr_…" (only the sha256 is stored, with created_at / expires_at)
pairing --> devtab : approved
phone -> ingest : GET /pair/{request_id}
ingest -> pairing : collect(request_id)
pairing --> ingest : {status: approved, token} (handed over once)
ingest --> phone : token
phone -> phone : keep the token in localStorage

== Stream ==
phone -> ingest : WebSocket /ws/stream/{device}
phone -> ingest : {"type": "auth", "token": "bsr_…"} as the first message
ingest -> tokens : verify(device, token)
alt valid and not expired
  tokens --> ingest : ok
  ingest --> phone : accepted, frames flow (see async_ingest)
else wrong, expired, revoked, or ?token= in the URL
  ingest --> phone : close 1008 (policy violation)
  phone --> user : "pair again from the Devices tab"
end

== Later ==
user -> devtab : Revoke device
devtab -> tokens : revoke(device)
note right of tokens
  devices.json is written with a per-file lock,
  a temp file, fsync and an atomic replace.
  Tokens are never logged (RedactSecretsFilter).
end note
@enduml
